Voice quality gate speech corpus
================================

Licence: public domain.

The four clips in this directory are cut from LibriVox recordings. LibriVox
releases its recordings into the public domain. The Internet Archive items
carry the Creative Commons Public Domain Mark 1.0:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/

| File              | Reader            | Voice  | Source item (Internet Archive)                     | Source file                    | Start (s) | Length (s) |
|-------------------|-------------------|--------|----------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|-----------|------------|
| m1_davison.wav    | Daniel Davison    | male   | https://archive.org/details/ss091_2007_librivox    | ss091_05_various_128kb.mp3     | 53.12     | 11.46      |
| f1_farris.wav     | Laurell Farris    | female | https://archive.org/details/ss091_2007_librivox    | ss091_14_various_128kb.mp3     | 64.74     | 10.00      |
| m2_grothmann.wav  | Dale Grothmann    | male   | https://archive.org/details/ss091_2007_librivox    | ss091_07_various_128kb.mp3     | 40.64     | 10.06      |
| f2_patterson.wav  | Mari Patterson    | female | https://archive.org/details/ss074_1810_librivox    | SS074_19_various_128kb.mp3     | 70.44     | 10.98      |

Catalog pages with the reader of each section:
- https://librivox.org/short-story-collection-91-by-various/
- https://librivox.org/short-story-collection-vol-074-by-various/

Processing (one time, 2026-10-06):
1. Decode the 128 kbps MP3 with ffmpeg, downmix to mono, resample to 48 kHz.
2. Cut at the start and length above. Each cut point is inside a pause.
3. Scale each clip to an active speech level of -26 dBFS (mean power of the
   20 ms frames within 30 dB of the loudest frame).
4. Apply a 10 ms linear fade in and fade out.
5. Write 48 kHz mono 16-bit PCM WAV.

The corpus is frozen. The voice quality baseline
(benchmarks/baselines/voice/baseline-2.9.json) was taken with these exact
files. A change to any file makes old and new scores incomparable: take the
baseline again on the commit the old baseline came from.
